## 52. SPECIAL PROVISIONS FOR JAMMU AND KASHMIR (HISTORICAL)

**[SYL: GS2-G.1] | [LAXMIKANTH: Chapter 52] | [ARTICLE 370 - HISTORICAL]**

### 52.1. Background

- **Accession**: Maharaja Hari Singh acceded to India on **26 October 1947** by signing Instrument of Accession (limited to defence, foreign affairs, communications).
- **Article 370**: Incorporated in Constitution as a **temporary provision** (Part XXI - Temporary, Transitional and Special Provisions) granting special autonomy to Jammu and Kashmir.
- **Constitution of J&K**: Adopted by J&K Constituent Assembly on **17 November 1956**, came into force on **26 January 1957**.

