42114-MEANING AND TYPES
42115-Political parties are voluntary associations or organised groups of
42116-individuals who share the same political views and who try to gain
42117-political power through constitutional means and who desire to
42118-work for promoting the national interest. There are four types of
42119-political parties in the modern democratic states, viz., (i)
42120-reactionary parties which cling to the old socio-economic and
42121-political institutions; (ii) conservative parties which believe in the
42122-status-quo; (iii) liberal parties which aim at reforming the existing
42123-institutions; and (iv) radical parties which aim at establishing a
42124-new order by overthrowing the existing institutions. In their
42125-classification of political parties on the basis of ideologies, the
42126-political scientists have placed the radical parties on the left and
42127-the liberal parties in the centre and reactionary and conservative
42128-parties on the right. In other words, they are described as the
42129-leftist parties, centrist parties and the rightist parties. In India, the
42130-CPI and CPM are the examples of leftist parties, the Congress of
42131-centrist parties and the BJP is an example of rightist parties.
42132-There are three kinds of party systems in the world, viz., (i) one
42133-party system in which only one ruling party exists and no
42134-opposition is permitted, as for example, in the former communist
42135-countries like the USSR and other East European countries; (ii)
42136-two-party system in which two major parties exists, as for
42137-example, in USA and Britain1 ; and (iii) multi-party system in which
42138-there are a number of political parties leading to the formation of
42139-coalition governments, as for example, in France, Switzerland and
42140-Italy.
42141-
42142-PARTY SYSTEM IN INDIA
42143-The Indian party system has the following characteristic features:
42144-
42145-Multi-Party System
42146-The continental size of the country, the diversified character of
42147-Indian society, the adoption of universal adult franchise, the
42148-peculiar type of political process, and other factors have given rise
42149-to a large number of political parties. In fact, India has the largest
42150-number of political parties in the world. On the eve of seventeenth
42151-Lok Sabha general elections (2019), there were 7 national parties,
42152-52 state parties and 2354 registered - unrecognised parties in the
42153-country2. Further, India has all categories of parties–left parties,
42154-centrist parties, right parties, communal parties, non-communal
42155-parties and so on. Consequently, the hung Parliaments, hung
42156-assemblies and coalition governments have become a common
42157-phenomena.
42158-
42159-One-Dominant Party System
42160-In spite of the multiparty system, the political scene in India was
