## 53. ELECTIONS

**[SYL: GS2-G.2] | [LAXMIKANTH: Chapter 71] | [ELECTORAL PROCESS, ECI, REPRESENTATION OF PEOPLE ACTS]**

### 53.1. Constitutional Provisions (Part XV)
- **Article 324**: Superintendence, direction and control of elections to Parliament, State Legislatures, offices of President and Vice-President vested in **Election Commission of India (ECI)**.
- **Articles 325-326**: No person ineligible on grounds of religion/race/caste/sex; **adult suffrage** (21 years reduced to 18 by **61st Amendment Act, 1988**, effective 1989).
- **Articles 327-328**: Parliament empowers to make laws for elections to Parliament/State Legislatures; State Legislatures for elections to their own Houses (subject to Parliament law).

### 53.2. Election Commission of India (ECI)
- **Constitutional Body**: Independent, permanent (Art. 324).
- **Composition**: Chief Election Commissioner (CEC) + other Election Commissioners as determined by President by law.
- **Appointment**: By President; since **1995** CEC and ECs appointed by President on recommendation of a Committee (traditionally PM, LoP, Law Minister) - now governed by **Chief Election Commissioner and Other Election Commissioners (Appointment, Conditions of Service and Term of Office) Act, 2023**.
- **Tenure & Removal**: CEC removed like Supreme Court Judge (impeachment - Art. 324(5)); other ECs removed on recommendation of CEC.
- **Powers & Functions**: Delimitation of constituencies (in consultation with State Election Commissions where relevant), preparation of electoral rolls, conduct of elections, recognition of political parties/symbols, model code of conduct enforcement, advise on disqualification (Art. 103, 192), election expenditure monitoring, etc.

### 53.3. Electoral System in India
- **First-Past-The-Post (FPTP)**: Simple majority system for Lok Sabha and State Legislative Assemblies.
- **Proportional Representation**: By Single Transferable Vote (STV) for Rajya Sabha, State Legislative Councils (where applicable), and election of President/Vice-President.
- **Reservation**: Seats reserved for SCs/STs in Lok Sabha/State Assemblies as per Delimitation Acts; **33% reservation for women** in PRIs (73rd/74th Amendments) and **Nari Shakti Vandan Adhiniyam, 2023** provides 33% reservation for women in Lok Sabha and State Assemblies (to come into effect after delimitation).

### 53.4. Delimitation of Constituencies
- **Delimitation Commission**: Constituted by Act of Parliament under Art. 82/170; orders have force of law, not ordinarily subject to judicial review.
- **Key Acts**: Delimitation Acts of 1952, 1962, 1972, 2002. **84th Amendment Act, 2001** froze delimitation until first census after 2026; **87th Amendment Act, 2003** allowed delimitation of constituencies on basis of 2001 census for SC/ST reservation only.
- **Freeze**: To protect federal balance, delimitation frozen till after 2026 census.

### 53.5. Anti-Defection Law (52nd Amendment Act, 1985)
- **Tenth Schedule**: Added by 52nd Amendment (1985); **91st Amendment Act, 2003** tightened provisions.
- **Grounds for disqualification**: Voluntarily gives up party membership OR votes/abstains contrary to party whip without prior permission (exceptions: merger - 2/3 members; split clause removed by 91st Amendment).
- **Decision**: By Speaker/Chairman of House; subject to judicial review on grounds of **malafides, perversity, or violation of constitutional provisions** (*Kihoto Hollohan v. Zachillhu*, 1992).
- **Effect**: Defecting MLAs/MPs disqualified; by-elections may follow.

### 53.6. Electoral Reforms (Key Measures)
- **Electoral rolls**: Photo Electoral Rolls, EPIC (Elector Photo Identity Card), Booth Level Officers, online voter registration.
- **Voting**: EVMs (since 1982, widespread since 1998), VVPAT introduced (*Subramanian Swamy v. ECI*, 2013 led to phased implementation), NOTA introduced by SC in ***PUCL v. Union of India*** (2013).
- **Transparency**: Election affidavits (criminal antecedents, assets, liabilities, education) - mandated by SC (*Union of India v. Association for Democratic Reforms*, 2002), implemented via Representation of People Act amendments.
- **Regulation**: Model Code of Conduct, expenditure limits, ceiling on party expenditure (no statutory ceiling but monitored), disclosure requirements, **Electoral Bonds** scheme introduced 2018 (later struck down by SC in ***Association for Democratic Reforms v. Union of India***, 2024).
- **Other**: Prohibition on exit polls during polling hours, paid news monitoring, use of Social Media platforms for transparency, **Remote Voting** discussions ongoing, **Voting for NRI** via postal ballot/electronic (limited).

### 53.7. Representation of the People Acts
- **RPA, 1950**: Preparation of electoral rolls, delimitation of constituencies.
- **RPA, 1951**: Conduct of elections, qualifications/disqualifications, corrupt practices, election petitions, by-elections.

